WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
Good morning, John.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.860
It’s Friday.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.480
Not just any Friday, my darling John; it is
Friday, 11/11.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.240
What’s the big deal about that?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.920
I have no idea, but sometimes, 11:11 is a
time where you see people tweet, “Make a

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.460
wish!” and I have no idea why, and I could
Google it right now, but frankly, I can’t be bothered.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.020
But why can’t I be bothered?

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:25.940
Because it’s also the first Friday of President-Elect
Trump’s president-electionry.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.180
President-electioncy?

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:27.740
I don’t know.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.471
Yes, that’s right everybody, we voted for
Donald Trump to be President!

00:00:30.471 --> 00:00:31.760
I didn’t in particular.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.600
I don’t know how many of you did, but people
did.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.480
Some people voted for Donald Trump to be President.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.520
Moreover, 46% of people didn’t vote at all.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.860
For those of you that don’t know who I am,
my name is Hannah Hart.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.769
I have a YouTube channel called Harto.

00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:50.600
I am most well known for a show called My
Drunk Kitchen, and most beloved for putting

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.660
my feelings all over the internet.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.140
But I don’t want to talk about me or how
incredible I am.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.699
I want to talk about the trouble with wishing,
because it occurs to me that wishes are what

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:05.910
got us here, and it occurs to me that wishing
is what made 46% of our population not vote.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.590
But let’s talk about the good thing about
wishes.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.830
What a wish is is your heart’s desires.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.460
It’s what you truly want.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.010
It’s what you truly want to be true.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.260
It’s what you truly want to see.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.110
It’s what you truly want to do.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.970
So in that way, a wish is a great thing because
it shows you things about yourself you might

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:20.970
not otherwise know.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.730
What’s the trouble with this wonderful thing?

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:29.250
Well, it gets you into something called wishful
thinking, where you think you can do less

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.520
and still get what you want.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.930
Now I don’t want to blame us for what just
happened, but I am going to blame us.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.040
Yeah, I know.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.500
It’s not our fault, but also, maybe it is.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.280
So in terms of ourselves and our hopes and
wishes and dreams and trying to turn those

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.280
thoughts into actions and those actions into
events of change, I think we probably took

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:54.310
that action for ourselves, but what I worry
we didn’t do is have enough conversations

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:59.220
with other people in our families.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.270
I’m just gonna say that.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.760
It’s a beautiful and wonderful thing that
we were motivated enough to vote as millennials

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:08.430
this year, that we had such a strong turnout,
and I think that the next step is talking

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:13.069
to those members of our family and the people
in our lives who perhaps hold alternative

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:17.239
political beliefs to ours or live in a world
of apathy.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:21.659
I am confident that there is someone in your
family that voted for Donald Trump and/or

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:22.690
didn’t vote at all.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:27.209
On a positive note, I do think it is an extraordinary
thing to live in a country where we can still

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:32.230
act in accordance with our beliefs, and while
we can still do so, I think we should.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.939
While it is still safe for us to have these
uncomfortable dinner conversations, I would

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:37.120
like you to do so.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.879
If there is a member of your family that you
know has opposing political beliefs to you,

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:45.659
I know it is awkward, but show them your Twitter
feed.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:50.020
Show them the instances of racism and violence
that are already being incited in quote-unquote

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.040
Trump’s America.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.660
If you have a friend that did not vote, show
them this, and if they’re like, “Well

00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:00.999
that wasn’t me; I didn’t vote for Trump,”
tell them, “But you didn’t vote at all.”

00:03:00.999 --> 00:03:03.170
Therefore, they are guilty by association.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:08.310
I know you would like to pretend like your
actions don’t matter, but sorry, your actions

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.010
and inactions matter a lot.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:16.420
So while we take this time to heal and mourn
and grieve, which I implore you to do so because

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.970
to rebuild your strength, you really need
to rest for a second, I also would like to

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.090
caution you to stay away from wishful thinking.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:29.560
It turns out that what we thought was enough
isn’t enough, so we can’t cross our fingers

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.560
for next time.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.779
We can’t cross our fingers that in two years
we’re gonna elect a congress more in line

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:34.969
with our beliefs.

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:37.649
We have to start having those conversations
now.

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:39.569
And John, I’ll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:41.620
Or at youtube.com/harto.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.220
Also, I hope you guys enjoyed this dramatic
lighting.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.960
It is a dramatic time, which is so exciting.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.720
Mwah.

